  "name": "Question 7",
  "problem": "In a table, each cell was colored either yellow or green. The ratio of yellow cells to the total number of cells is $2:3.$ If there are $24$ yellow cells, how many cells were colored green?",
  "worked_solution": "We are given that the ratio of yellow cells to the total number of cells is $\\frac{2}{3}.$ \n\nIn this fraction, the numerator represents the number of yellow cells, and the denominator represents the total number of cells.\n\nWe can make a numerator of $24$ by multiplying the numerator and denominator by $12:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{2\\times 12}{3\\times 12}=\\frac{24}{36}\n$$\n\nTherefore, there are a total of $36$ cells in the table. \nSo, the number of green cells is\n\n$$\n36-24=12.\n$$",
